According to jbovlaste, the fraction slash { fi'u } by itself means the golden
ratio <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_ratio>, commonly denoted phi, and
when used as { fi'u x } is shorthand for { pa fi'u x }. So then li fi'u vu'u
fi'u fi'u is phi - 1/phi which does in fact equal one.

Where this convention comes from though, I don't know.

mu'omi'e .ros.

